      "writtenOn": "2024-04-12T05:32:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve checked RM0433 for STM32H743 (dartmonkey) and there are no D3 bits in `DBGMCU_CR` definition - https://screenshot.googleplex.com/BcwJgW5w5YTmMa3.\n\nHAL says [the same](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/hal_stm32/stm32cube/stm32h7xx/soc/stm32h743xx.h;l\u003d21134).\n\nHowever some H7 chips indeed [define](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyr/hal_stm32/stm32cube/stm32h7xx/soc/stm32h723xx.h;l\u003d21566) the D3 bits. I should probably change the `elif` to a specific chip. What do you think?",
